00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:09,840
still be a prey to suffering there. But also, once\h
this is seen, that safety cannot leave you.

120
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:14,800
So wherever you go in the "external world", you'll\h
be safe because it is that relationship between

121
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:19,840
you and your own mind that is the determining\h
factor here. Yes.

122
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:26,320
And you would see it in the suttas when the Buddha\h
would say: Whatever form, whether past, present

123
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:35,600
or future, big or small, inferior or superior, 
it's in regard to all form that this attitude

124
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:40,720
has to be developed. In other words, the attitude\h
of dispassion, the attitude of non-ownership.

125
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:48,640
So then for somebody who doesn't see their own 
mind\hclearly, whether they like it or not, they will be

126
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:56,320
maintaining attitudes of passion in regard to some\h
form, some feeling, some perception, some intention

127
00:14:56,320 --> 00:15:07,920
some consciousness. So it's in regard to that\h
kind of... it's the most comprehensive scope where

128
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:16,400
nothing is left out, even as that suttas says: If you were\h
to perceive "nibbāna" and then because of thinking

