00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:53,743
Even if those doubts arise, again\hbecause you see 
the attitude in regard to whatever arises now,

159
00:18:53,743 --> 00:19:00,480
you wouldn't fall for it, and that's\hwhy the Buddha said, 
the mind that with ayoniso manasikāra, they would be

160
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:10,560
inevitably to some extent revolving around\h
questions of Who was I? Where did I come from?

161
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:16,960
What am I right now? Where will I become later?\h
Because you realize, even through the Buddhist\hteaching

162
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:22,400
you could be feeding those views. 
You could be using the pronouncements about X or Y

163
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:28,880
that the Buddha made, to revolve around your own\h
doubts of trying to explain things.

164
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:33,760
Thinking that somehow figuring things out will\h
resolve your suffering. Again, overlooking

165
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:39,920
"Well, what is my attitude in regard to all this doubting\h
and clarifying?" and you know, trying to get the\hanswers.

166
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:46,160
Is it an attitude of dispassion? Well,\h
realistically, most of the time it's not.

167
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:53,200
And seeing now the mind, which depends on\h
virtue and also seclusion you mentioned, that

168
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:58,240
doesn't actually now require explanation. 
There's no causal [relation] like, first this, then that,

