00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:29,680
but that's not what we're doing here. It is more\h
like what is necessary in order to recognize the mind,

174
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:36,080
which is already there, and that is not the\h
product of an explanation. It's more a quality of

175
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:42,080
the utterance of another being the right\h
description, but... that it points you to find it.

176
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:48,400
Yes. And then it depends on the listener\h
how far they take that description "inwards",

177
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:55,280
so that they actually see what is being\hdescribed. 
Well, the origin, like the yoniso, meaning

178
00:20:55,280 --> 00:21:06,160
the origin, like in the sense of, it being
the womb that kind of hovers over this whole\hthing.

179
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:12,640
This attitude that hovers over this\h
entire thing, that underlies it, that contains it.

180
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:20,000
And then, that's where the mind is. And that's where\h
you would be either – through your carelessness –

181
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:27,440
making it worse, when it's already in an unwholesome\h
state, or as wild as it might have gotten, if you

182
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:33,440
understood where it is, you would be able\h
to, first of all, see it as such; not lose

183
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:38,480
perspective in regard to that, as the satipaṭṭhāna sutta says,
even where your mind is lustful, you know:

184
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:47,520
the mind is lustful, and then you would be fully\h
capable of bringing it out of that state,

185
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:54,880
without having to wish and hope on random methods and\h
practices that worked in the past, and having to

186
00:21:54,880 --> 00:22:01,600
combine them and mix them and make new ones
or something, hoping that it will work again.

187
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:13,737
It's like, if that's your level of\hpractice,
then it's not much better than depending on the weather.

188
00:22:13,737 --> 00:22:18,240
If\hyou have understood your mind, you should be able to

189
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:25,760
abandon any unwholesome state. On the spot.\h
Yes. Well, not necessarily on the spot, but

190
00:22:25,760 --> 00:22:31,840
be beyond doubt about what has to be done in
order to abandon it. Because as the Buddha said,

191
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:36,720
it's a matter of feeding; you feed the\h
hindrances and you starve the hindrances.

192
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:43,280
Yes, which means that when you see your mind, in a sense,\h
that's also it. Yes. Because with that

193
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:49,600
will now come the knowledge how it's fed, right?\h
Yes. But even then, it wouldn't be like...\h

194
00:22:52,029 --> 00:22:58,261
basically, it's a certainty that you know\h
what to do. You still have to do it. If you...

195
00:22:58,261 --> 00:23:03,520
Yes, but the doing is to now\hnot feed... 
Yes. So then if

196
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:11,858
having seen your mind, you\hneed another step, 
that's because you don't see your mind.

197
00:23:11,858 --> 00:23:15,760
That's what I meant now by on the spot...
So\hthere's an immediacy to it. Yes. Exactly.

198
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:20,720
Because, you know, somebody could fall\h
into that view like: "Oh yes, I do see my mind"

199
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:28,720
and then I start doing XYZ, and it's like: 
Well,\hif you feel that that's required, you should be

200
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:33,120
cautious about whether you actually see your\h
mind or not. Because as the Buddha said,

201
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:40,240
it's through avijjā, that's the root\h
cause of the source of the\hwhole river.

202
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:45,752
So if you have actually undone your\havijjā, 
that should be able to fix the problem in and of itself.

203
00:23:45,752 --> 00:23:51,120
Yes. So we can say that ignorance,\h
avijjā, is in relation to the mind. Not knowing or

204
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:58,880
ignoring mind, is the problem of all this.
Yes. Because it's an either/or. You can't

205
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:08,800
be ignoring the mind and then going towards\h
the direction of wholesome; you can't be

206
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:15,013
seeing the mind and then still acting out of\h
greed, aversion and delusion. That's impossible.

